Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------

The changes cursor-plugin-cc made to the Grok Build plugin are listed in that
project's NOTICE file. Starting from cursor-plugin-cc 0.2.4 (commit 288c791),
this project made the following substantive changes:

  * The CLI adapter layer (`scripts/lib/cursor.mjs`) was replaced by
    `scripts/lib/agy.mjs`, which drives the Antigravity CLI (`agy`) instead of
    the Cursor CLI (`cursor-agent`).
  * Read-only execution no longer relies on a CLI mode. agy keeps tool
    permissions in a global settings file with no per-run override, so every
    run starts agy with a plugin-owned home directory and a permission profile
    (read-only / write / write-commands) written into that home under a lock.
    The permission mode agy reports at start-up is checked, and a run that did
    not get the profile is stopped.
  * The prompt moved from stdin (which agy ignores) to an attached `-p=` argument,
    with a prompt file in an added directory for long prompts and for Windows
    `.cmd` shims. `--disable-slash-commands` is always passed.
  * Output is read as `stream-json` events. agy's exit code and `SUCCESS`
    status are not trusted: refused permissions, print timeouts, empty answers
    and unknown conversation ids fail the run, and a turn that ended on a
    refused permission is continued once automatically.
  * Structured output uses agy's `--json-schema` flag and `structured_output`.
  * Sessions are agy conversation ids (`--conversation`); the authentication
    probe is `agy models`.
  * New options: `--effort`, `--timeout` (agy's `--print-timeout`),
    `--allow-commands`, and a repeatable `--add-dir`.
  * New command `/agy-cc:image`, which uses agy's built-in image generator and
    copies the result out of agy's conversation folder.
  * Review context is always collected by the bridge (agy cannot run git in a
    read-only run) with a larger inline budget.
  * Binary override renamed to `AGY_BINARY`, the session environment variable
    to `AGY_CC_SESSION_ID`, and all command, agent, skill, and marketplace
    identifiers renamed from `cursor-cc` to `agy-cc`.

